WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.334
-It's time to play a game
of deception

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.303
called "True Confessions."

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:11.977 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:13.012
Wow.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.281
My first opponent
is an amazing actor

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.416
whose new animated series,
"The Great North,"

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.586
airs Sundays at 8:30 p.m.
on FOX.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.622
Please welcome Nick Offerman.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.324
Nick, it is great to see you.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.193
-Thank you, Jimmy.
Good to see you.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.962
-Nick and I will be facing off
against a talented model

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:33.399
who just launched a brand-new
YouTube channel today.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.368
Please welcome Hailey Bieber.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.736
Oh!

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.471
Hailey, welcome, welcome,
welcome.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.538
I'm happy you guys are here.

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:40.907
Here's how this works.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:44.010
Each of us have two envelopes
containing confessions.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.078
One is true, the other is a lie.

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.781
Once you read your confession,

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.682
the other players
will interrogate you,

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.017
and then they have to come to
a unanimous decision --

00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:55.087
is it the truth or a lie?

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.622
Nick, you will go first.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.223
Hailey, which envelope
should he open,

00:00:58.223 --> 00:00:59.826
number one or number two?

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.863
-Number two.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.498
-Yeah, I agree.
-Number two.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.832
-Yep.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:09.068
-In a Tokyo --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.871
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.172
Who wrote these?

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:16.008
In a Tokyo hotel lobby,

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:20.947
I once offered my services
to a middle-aged businessman

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.515
as a prostitute.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.983 line:0%
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.786 line:0%
What?

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.655 line:0%
Wait, no.
What -- What --

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.491 line:0%
Alright, what year was this?

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.593 line:0%
-1991.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.530 line:0%
-And why were you in Tokyo?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:42.235 line:0%
-I was touring a Kabuki
theater show around Japan.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.171 line:0%
-Yeah. And you were in
the Kabuki theater?

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:51.778 line:0%
-I was. I was cast as...
soldier number three.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.079 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:58.317 line:0%
It's so outlandish that I feel
like it might be true.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.386 line:0%
-There was a language situation

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.188 line:0%
that maybe created
a bit of a snafu.

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:07.026 line:0%
-Ah. [ Laughs ]

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.695 line:0%
-I was going to say
there's no way that's true,

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:10.763 line:0%
but I don't know.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.700 line:0%
I think honestly
that now makes me think

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.901 line:0%
that it actually did happen.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.503 line:0%
Hailey, what do you think?

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.138 line:0%
-That's -- What I was saying
before is

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:22.341 line:0%
it sounds so outlandish
that perhaps it's true.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:23.676 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.843 line:0%
-You are correct.

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:26.378 line:0%
That actually did occur.
[ Ding ]

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:27.947 line:0%
-Yes!
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.482 line:0%
What happened?

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.716 line:0%
Wait. What did you think
you were saying?

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.451
-Yeah, what was going on here?

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:33.686
-My two friends and I

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.221
were having breakfast
in this hotel lobby,

00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:38.590
and they were also
in the show.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.426
And this older gentleman
came over,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.695
and he was very interested
to meet us.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.730
And we were trying to
make conversation,

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.234
and he was offering us
cigarettes.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.136
And we were smokers then,
so we took them.

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:53.406
And we kept saying
we're in the Kabuki show,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.074
and his eyes would light up.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.977
And so what happened was...
-[ Laughs ] What?

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.079
-...Kabuki is the theater style,

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:03.783
but it is also slang
for "prostitutes."

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.985
-Oh, wow!
-So we were saying to this guy,

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.887
"We're in a theater show,"

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.822
and what he was hearing is,
"Hello.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.858
We're American hookers.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.360
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.595
-It is now -- It is my turn.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:19.132
Which envelope should I open?

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.033
Number one, number two?
Do you care?

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.635
-I'll go number one.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.307
-Is that what you propositioned
to the guy?

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.176
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.315
Here we go.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:38.684
One time, I accidentally dined
and dashed with Alec Baldwin

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:41.254
because we each thought
the other person paid the bill.

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.524 line:0%
You know him.

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:48.627 line:0%
Questions?

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:50.062 line:0%
-Doesn't seem impossible to me.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.263 line:0%
But here's what
I want to know --

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.399 line:0%
Where were you dining?

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.967 line:0%
-It was Pierre's,

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:58.371 line:0%
which is a French bistro
in East Hampton.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:01.574 line:0%
-Oh, you're good.
That's a good detail.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:05.645 line:0%
-So, Hailey, you know this turf,
I presume.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.913 line:0%
-Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.048 line:0%
I feel like I should have
a sixth sense

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.851 line:0%
because this is someone
I'm related to.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:14.020 line:0%
Um...hmm.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.155 line:0%
I'm going to say

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.958
that I think
that that's probably true.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.793
-I'm going to say it's true.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.294 line:0%
-It's false.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:23.762 line:0%
-[ Gasps ]
-What?!

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:27.333 line:0%
-That's the best acting
I've ever done in my life!

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.667 line:0%
We would nev--

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.569
I've been to dinner with Alec,
but, no,

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.871
we never dined and dashed
at Pierre's.

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:34.807
I made the whole thing up.
-You said it was an accident!

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.943
-I made the whole thing up!

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.678
-Wow, you are diabolical, Jimmy.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.413
-Never, ever, ever happened.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.982
Yes!
That's the greatest acting.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.550
I should get back into movies.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.686
-I'm impressed. I'm impressed.
-Thank you.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.387
Hailey, it is now your turn.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.355
Nick, which envelope
should she open --

00:04:50.355 --> 00:04:53.059
number one or number two?

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.194
-I will go with number two,
please.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.363
-Yep.
-Number two, okay.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.800
[ Sighs ]

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.802
Number two says...

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:06.005
one time,
I got lost on a jet ski

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:09.075
and was chased
by a pack of wild dogs.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.844 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.345 line:0%
-Okay.
-Phew.

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:14.747 line:0%
-I know. That's a thinker.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.949 line:0%
It's a brain bender
only because --

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.217 line:0%
I'm just not seeing
the wild dogs

00:05:19.217 --> 00:05:21.954 line:0%
on the water chasing you.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.923 line:0%
And they have to be
running pretty fast

00:05:24.923 --> 00:05:28.828 line:0%
to be chasing you on a jet ski,
wouldn't you say, Nick?

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.563 line:0%
-Well, unless --

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:36.669 line:0%
are "The Wild Dogs"
the name of a marauding gang...

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.704 line:0%
-[ Laughs ] Like a jet ski gang?

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.940 line:0%
-...in the Hampton area,
perhaps?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.141 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.141 --> 00:05:45.545 line:0%
-The Wild Dogs. Yeah,
they're a famous jet ski gang.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:49.314 line:0%
I've heard of these.
They're like a lake gang.

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:53.285 line:0%
-No, we're talking
real, live wild dogs.

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:54.954 line:0%
-Was it night or day?

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.156 line:0%
-What are you talking --
-It was daytime.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.691 line:0%
-You can't jet ski at nighttime.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.793 line:0%
-Jet skiing at night
sounds dangerous.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.894 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.397 line:0%
-I'm not a big
jet ski enthusiast.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.432 line:0%
I apologize.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.601 line:0%
You --

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.503 line:0%
Did you survive the encounter?

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:12.404 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:13.472 line:0%
Obviously.

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:14.340 line:0%
Alright. Wait a second.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.641 line:0%
-Well, I'm here.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.909 line:0%
-Yes, you're here.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.378 line:0%
Well, how did you get to land?

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.014 line:0%
I'm assuming they chased you
around the beach.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:28.954 line:0%
-We were actually doing
a little boat excursion,

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:31.590 line:0%
and we had taken the jet skis
off the boat...

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.159 line:0%
-Okay. Alright. Here we go.
-...to explore,

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:38.464 line:0%
and we ended up just barely
making it back

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:41.467 line:0%
after a few of the jet skis
had died.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:44.470 line:0%
-Yep. This is --
You know why this is true?

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.607 line:0%
Nick?
Because I was a model myself,

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:53.112 line:0%
and when you are successful,
you do -- you party.

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:56.648 line:0%
-Okay. Jimmy,
did I hear correctly?

00:06:56.648 --> 00:06:59.986 line:0%
Are you attempting to tell me
what models do?

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:02.355 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:06.292 line:0%
As though I'm not a very --

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:08.361 line:0%
-No, no, no, no, no, no,
I would never say that.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:11.130 line:0%
That is not -- Dude, no no.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.099 line:0%
I would never --
Sorry to insult you.

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:16.601 line:0%
Dude, I've known you
for a long time. So --

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:21.140 line:0%
-I'm -- Listen, I mean, I guess
I'm either gullible

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.775 line:0%
or you guys are very talented,

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:26.879 line:0%
because I'm also leaning towards
believing this story.

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:30.917 line:0%
And also, I'm just going to text
my business manager real quick

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:32.918 line:0%
because I'm going to invent

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:34.920 line:0%
a jet ski with a headlight
and --

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.355 line:0%
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.157 line:0%
That's not the point
of all of this!

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.658 line:0%
-Get the [bleep]

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:43.295 line:0%
-Chased by wild dogs
on a jet ski,

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:46.164 line:0%
which is, honestly,
that is an insane story.

00:07:46.164 --> 00:07:49.134 line:0%
I'm going to say it sounds
so bizarre that it's true.

00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:51.736 line:0%
-I agree. We say true.

00:07:51.736 --> 00:07:53.305 line:0%
-You guys are correct.

00:07:53.305 --> 00:07:56.142 line:0%
[ Laughing ]
That is a true story.

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:59.145
-My thanks to Nick Offerman,
Hailey Bieber.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.179
That was "True Confessions."

